codex
The fresh LLVM concrete build exposed two important issues. First, its `[concrete]`-guarded `noDivisors` equations do not execute under LLVM, so nontrivial runs stop; I’m rebuilding the concrete definition with the Haskell backend used by the submission to distinguish backend portability from theorem soundness. Second, K’s `lengthString` is visibly counting UTF-8 bytes (`"😀😀"` became 8 and `"你好"` became 6), unlike Python `len(str)`, which counts Unicode code points. I’m testing that discrepancy end-to-end because it may be a decisive real-program semantics defect.
