codex
The rule-by-rule review confirms the decisive defect is localized and witnessed: `valueLength(VStr(S)) => lengthString(S)` is not a valid semantics for Python `len(str)` on the intended Unicode domain. The fresh false-postcondition mutation also behaved correctly—it parsed/build-dried successfully, then failed with a result-equality residual—so the claim is not vacuous; non-vacuity does not cure the wrong language model.
The exhaustive inventory identified one materially unsound Python/K bridge with concrete witnesses; the fresh negated-result mutation built and failed for the expected obligation.
